/*
  core/masks/attentive_share.spthy -- f_H for the Attentive mask, SHARE_PW action.
  (Action-scoped, per repo MEMORY.md lesson 3: include only in a ceremony that has a SHARE_PW
   request, else the !Req premise is unproduced -- a hard wellformedness failure.)

  The Attentive sender follows the guide: the passphrase travels over a channel OTHER than the
  email. We model that side channel as the PRIVATE linear fact Oob(P,recip,pw), which the
  Dolev-Yao adversary cannot read -- so an Attentive share never puts pw on the wire. RespMask
  (P,'Attentive') is gated by core/transitions/mask_state.spthy: valid only when no degrade is active.
*/

rule Share_Attentive:
    [ !Req(P, rid, 'SHARE_PW', <recip, pw>, c) ]
  --[ Share(P,'Attentive'), RespMask(P,'Attentive'), Answered(rid), ShareOOB(P, recip) ]->
    [ Oob(P, recip, pw) ]
